## Course overview

The **School-Supported Self-Taught (SSST)** option lets a student study **Language A: Literature at SL** in a first language that the school does not teach. Students work largely independently on a personalised reading list, with the school providing structure, supervision, and support toward the assessments.

This keeps a bilingual diploma within reach for students whose mother tongue falls outside the school's taught Group 1 offerings.

## What you will study

- A **personalised list of literary works** in the chosen language, agreed with the school's supervisor.
- **Readers, writers and texts**, **time and space**, and **intertextuality** - the same concepts as the taught Literature course.
- **Works in translation** alongside works originally written in the chosen language.

## Assessment

| Component | SL | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 (guided literary analysis) | 35% | Guided analysis of an unseen literary passage |
| Paper 2 (comparative essay) | 35% | Comparison of two studied literary works |
| Individual Oral | 30% | Spoken analysis of two literary works |
